# Kiro CLI. Model traffic and account state go to the hosts of the profile's region. Kiro offers two regions,
# us-east-1 and eu-central-1.
# - runtime serves inference.
# - management serves the profile and subscription state.
# - The legacy q.<region> host is required beside runtime and management.
# The CLI tab of https://kiro.dev/docs/privacy-and-security/firewalls/ lists these hosts with their purposes.
allow https://runtime.us-east-1.kiro.dev/       tunnel
allow https://management.us-east-1.kiro.dev/    tunnel
allow https://q.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/        tunnel
allow https://runtime.eu-central-1.kiro.dev/    tunnel
allow https://management.eu-central-1.kiro.dev/ tunnel
allow https://q.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/     tunnel

# Sign-in, `kiro-cli login --use-device-flow`: the CLI prints the code, and the browser approves the code. The CLI
# then polls for the tokens and refreshes them at a host that depends on the account kind.
# - Google and GitHub accounts use Kiro's own host, plus the Cognito federation that the same page lists for them.
# - Builder ID and IAM Identity Center use AWS SSO OIDC in the instance's region. Builder ID's region is us-east-1.
# - An Identity Center in another region needs a workspace's own `allow https://oidc.<region>.amazonaws.com/ tunnel`
#   line. Without the line, the sign-in fails with `error: dispatch failure`, and the proxy log names the refused
#   host.
allow https://prod.us-east-1.auth.desktop.kiro.dev/     tunnel
allow https://cognito-identity.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/ tunnel
allow https://oidc.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/             tunnel

# These hosts of the same list are absent:
# - telemetry.<region>.kiro.dev and prod.us-east-1.telemetry.desktop.kiro.dev receive telemetry. Each attempt leaves
#   a refusal in the log, or none with `kiro-cli settings telemetry.enabled false`.
# - prod.download.cli.kiro.dev and desktop-release.q.us-east-1.amazonaws.com serve updates and installer downloads,
#   which the image turns off (app.disableAutoupdates).
# - cli.kiro.dev serves the install script.
